    "question": "Tim decides to start selling necklaces he makes.  He uses 10 charms to make each necklace.  Each charm cost $15.  He sells the necklace for $200.  How much profit does he make if he sells 30?",
    "gold": "1500",
    "answer": "Each necklace cost 10*15=$<<10*15=150>>150 to make\nSo he makes a profit of 200-150=$<<200-150=50>>50 each\nSo his total profit is 50*30=$<<50*30=1500>>1500\n#### 1500"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine Tim's profit, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the charms used to make one necklace.\n2. Determine the total revenue from selling one necklace.\n3. Calculate the profit by subtracting the total cost from the total revenue.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the charms used to make one necklace.**\n\nEach necklace uses 10 charms, and each charm costs $15. Therefore, the cost of the charms for one necklace is:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ charms} \\times 15 \\text{ dollars/charm} = 150 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total revenue from selling one necklace.**\n\nTim sells each necklace for $200. Therefore, the revenue from selling one necklace is:\n\\[ 200 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the profit by subtracting the total cost from the total revenue.**\n\nThe profit is calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{Profit} = \\text{Total Revenue} - \\text{Total Cost} = 200 \\text{ dollars} - 150 \\text{ dollars} = 50 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nSince Tim sells 30 necklaces, the total profit is:\n\\[ 30 \\times 50 \\text{ dollars} = 1500 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the profit Tim makes if he sells 30 necklaces is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1500} \\]",
